/* lesson text for sc: id -> [[EN lines...], [MS lines...]] (loaded on demand) */
export default {
"sc_sense": [["We have five senses. Eyes see, ears hear, a nose smells, a tongue tastes and skin feels. Senses tell us about the world.","Smell the pandan leaf in a kuih: that is your nose. Taste a sweet mango and a sour lime: that is your tongue. Both are different tastes.","Touch a soft pillow, a rough coconut husk and a prickly rambutan. Your skin feels soft, rough and prickly.","Try it: Close your eyes. Ask a friend to hold something near you. Use your nose, ears and hands to guess what it is.","Tip: Five senses, five fingers on one hand. Count them: see, hear, smell, taste, touch.","Fun fact: When your nose is blocked by a cold, food tastes plain. Your nose and tongue work together to taste food."],["Kita ada lima pancaindera. Mata melihat, telinga mendengar, hidung menghidu, lidah merasa dan kulit menyentuh. Pancaindera memberitahu kita tentang dunia.","Hidu daun pandan dalam kuih: itu hidung kamu. Rasa mangga yang manis dan limau yang masam: itu lidah kamu. Kedua-duanya rasa yang berbeza.","Sentuh bantal yang lembut, sabut kelapa yang kasar dan rambutan yang berduri. Kulit kamu merasa lembut, kasar dan berduri.","Cuba ini: Pejam mata. Minta kawan memegang sesuatu berhampiran kamu. Guna hidung, telinga dan tangan untuk meneka apa itu.","Tip: Lima pancaindera, lima jari pada satu tangan. Kira: lihat, dengar, hidu, rasa, sentuh.","Fakta menarik: Apabila hidung tersumbat kerana selesema, makanan terasa tawar. Hidung dan lidah bekerjasama untuk merasa makanan."]],
"sc_animal": [["Animals move in different ways. Their bodies are made for the way they move. Some fly, some swim, some walk and some crawl.","A bird flies with two wings. A fish swims with fins and a tail. A cat walks on four legs and a snake slides on its belly.","A frog hops on strong back legs. A snail glides slowly on one foot and leaves a shiny trail behind it.","Try it: Move like each animal for 10 seconds. Flap like a bird, wiggle like a fish and hop like a frog. Which one is the hardest?","Tip: Wings fly, fins swim, legs walk. Match the body part to the move.","Fun fact: A kangaroo cannot walk backwards easily, but a crab walks sideways. Animals move in surprising ways!"],["Haiwan bergerak dengan cara yang berbeza. Badan mereka sesuai dengan cara mereka bergerak. Ada yang terbang, berenang, berjalan dan merayap.","Burung terbang dengan dua sayap. Ikan berenang dengan sirip dan ekor. Kucing berjalan dengan empat kaki dan ular menyusur di atas perutnya.","Katak melompat dengan kaki belakang yang kuat. Siput bergerak perlahan di atas satu kaki dan meninggalkan jejak berkilat di belakangnya.","Cuba ini: Bergerak seperti setiap haiwan selama 10 saat. Kepak seperti burung, geliat seperti ikan dan lompat seperti katak. Yang mana paling susah?","Tip: Sayap terbang, sirip berenang, kaki berjalan. Padankan anggota badan dengan gerakan.","Fakta menarik: Kanggaru tidak mudah berjalan ke belakang, tetapi ketam berjalan ke sisi. Haiwan bergerak dengan cara yang mengejutkan!"]],
"sc_day": [["We have day and night because the Earth spins slowly like a top. The side facing the Sun has day. The side turned away has night.","In the morning we see the Sun rise. At noon it is high and bright. In the evening it sets, and the sky goes dark.","Our day and night take 24 hours. In Malaysia, day is about 12 hours long and night is about 12 hours long all year round.","Try it: In a dark room, shine a torch on a ball. The lit side is day. Turn the ball slowly and see day change to night.","Tip: The Earth turns, the Sun stays still. Spin makes the Sun seem to move.","Fun fact: Owls and bats wake up at night to hunt for food. We call them nocturnal animals."],["Kita ada siang dan malam kerana Bumi berputar perlahan seperti gasing. Bahagian yang menghadap Matahari ialah siang. Bahagian yang membelakangi Matahari ialah malam.","Pada waktu pagi kita nampak Matahari terbit. Pada waktu tengah hari ia tinggi dan terang. Pada waktu petang ia terbenam dan langit menjadi gelap.","Satu siang dan satu malam mengambil masa 24 jam. Di Malaysia, siang kira-kira 12 jam dan malam kira-kira 12 jam sepanjang tahun.","Cuba ini: Dalam bilik gelap, suluh bola dengan lampu suluh. Bahagian yang terang ialah siang. Putar bola perlahan-lahan dan lihat siang bertukar menjadi malam.","Tip: Bumi yang berputar, Matahari tidak bergerak. Putaran membuat Matahari nampak bergerak.","Fakta menarik: Burung hantu dan kelawar bangun pada waktu malam untuk mencari makanan. Kita panggil mereka haiwan nokturnal."]],
"sc_life": [["A life cycle shows how a living thing grows and changes from a baby to a grown-up. Then the grown-up has babies, and the cycle starts again.","A butterfly goes through 4 stages: egg, caterpillar, pupa and butterfly. Inside the pupa the caterpillar changes into a butterfly.","A frog also changes: egg, tadpole with a tail, froglet with legs, then a frog. Tadpoles live in water and frogs live on land too.","Try it: Draw a circle with 4 boxes. Draw the stages of a butterfly or frog in order. Add arrows going around the circle.","Tip: A cycle goes round and round, with no end. Say the stages in order, then say them again.","Fun fact: A hen sits on her eggs for about 21 days until the chicks hatch. Careful: The pupa is not sleeping. It is changing!"],["Kitar hidup menunjukkan bagaimana benda hidup membesar dan berubah daripada bayi kepada dewasa. Kemudian yang dewasa mempunyai anak dan kitar itu bermula lagi.","Rama-rama melalui 4 peringkat: telur, ulat, kepompong dan rama-rama. Di dalam kepompong, ulat berubah menjadi rama-rama.","Katak juga berubah: telur, berudu berekor, katak kecil berkaki, kemudian katak dewasa. Berudu hidup dalam air dan katak boleh hidup di darat juga.","Cuba ini: Lukis bulatan dengan 4 kotak. Lukis peringkat rama-rama atau katak mengikut turutan. Tambah anak panah mengelilingi bulatan.","Tip: Kitaran berpusing tanpa penghujung. Sebut peringkat mengikut turutan, kemudian sebut lagi.","Fakta menarik: Ayam betina mengeram telur kira-kira 21 hari sehingga anak ayam menetas. Awas: Kepompong tidak tidur. Ia sedang berubah!"]],
"sc_water": [["Water moves around the Earth again and again. It goes up into the sky, forms clouds, falls as rain and flows back to the sea. This is the water cycle.","After rain, a puddle on the road slowly gets smaller. The Sun warms the water and it goes up into the air as vapour. This is evaporation.","High in the sky, the vapour cools into tiny drops of water that make clouds. This is condensation. When drops get heavy they fall as rain.","Try it: Fill a glass with cold water and ice. Wait 5 minutes. Water drops appear on the outside. They came from vapour in the air!","Tip: Up, cloud, down, flow. Evaporate, condense, rain, collect in rivers and seas.","Fun fact: The water you drink is very, very old. The same water has been going round the Earth for millions of years."],["Air bergerak mengelilingi Bumi berulang kali. Ia naik ke langit, membentuk awan, turun sebagai hujan dan mengalir semula ke laut. Ini ialah kitaran air.","Selepas hujan, lopak di jalan perlahan-lahan mengecil. Matahari memanaskan air dan air naik ke udara sebagai wap. Ini ialah penyejatan.","Di langit tinggi, wap menyejuk menjadi titisan air kecil yang membentuk awan. Ini ialah kondensasi. Apabila titisan menjadi berat, ia turun sebagai hujan.","Cuba ini: Isi gelas dengan air sejuk dan ais. Tunggu 5 minit. Titisan air muncul di luar gelas. Ia datang daripada wap dalam udara!","Tip: Naik, awan, turun, mengalir. Sejat, kondensasi, hujan, terkumpul di sungai dan laut.","Fakta menarik: Air yang kamu minum sangat lama usianya. Air yang sama telah berputar mengelilingi Bumi berjuta-juta tahun."]],
"sc_body": [["Our body has many parts and each part has a job. We have a head on top, a neck, two arms, two hands, a tummy and two legs with feet.","Your brain is inside your head. It helps you think and remember. Your elbow bends your arm and your knee bends your leg.","Your heart is inside your chest. It pumps blood all around your body. Your lungs fill with air when you breathe in.","Try it: Put your hand on your chest and feel your heart go thump, thump. Now run on the spot for 20 seconds. Does it beat faster?","Tip: Sing the song: Head, shoulders, knees and toes, knees and toes! Touch each part as you sing.","Fun fact: A grown-up has 206 bones inside the body. Bones are hard and keep us standing tall."],["Badan kita mempunyai banyak bahagian dan setiap bahagian ada tugasnya. Kita ada kepala di atas, leher, dua lengan, dua tangan, perut dan dua kaki.","Otak kamu ada di dalam kepala. Ia membantu kamu berfikir dan mengingat. Siku membengkokkan lengan dan lutut membengkokkan kaki.","Jantung kamu ada di dalam dada. Ia mengepam darah ke seluruh badan. Paru-paru dipenuhi udara apabila kamu menarik nafas.","Cuba ini: Letak tangan di dada dan rasa jantung berdegup. Kemudian berlari di tempat selama 20 saat. Adakah ia berdegup lebih laju?","Tip: Nyanyi lagu ini: Kepala, bahu, lutut dan jari kaki! Sentuh setiap anggota semasa menyanyi.","Fakta menarik: Orang dewasa ada 206 tulang di dalam badan. Tulang itu keras dan membuat kita berdiri tegak."]],
"sc_food": [["Healthy food helps us grow, play and learn. Our bodies need many kinds of food: rice and bread, fish and eggs, fruit and vegetables.","Malaysia has a Healthy Plate called Suku Suku Separuh. Fill one quarter with rice, one quarter with fish, egg or meat, and half with fruit and vegetables.","A good breakfast can be a boiled egg, a banana and a glass of milk. It gives you energy for the whole morning at school.","Try it: Draw a plate with 4 parts. Colour half for fruit and vegetables. Draw your favourite foods in each part.","Tip: Eat a rainbow! Orange carrots, green kangkung, red tomatoes and yellow bananas all help your body.","Careful: Sweet drinks and sweets are treats, not everyday food. Plain water is the best drink. Fun fact: Over half of our body is water."],["Makanan sihat membantu kita membesar, bermain dan belajar. Badan kita perlukan pelbagai jenis makanan: nasi dan roti, ikan dan telur, buah dan sayur.","Malaysia ada Pinggan Sihat yang dipanggil Suku Suku Separuh. Isi satu suku dengan nasi, satu suku dengan ikan, telur atau daging, dan separuh dengan buah dan sayur.","Sarapan yang baik boleh jadi telur rebus, sebiji pisang dan segelas susu. Ia memberi tenaga untuk sepanjang pagi di sekolah.","Cuba ini: Lukis pinggan dengan 4 bahagian. Warnakan separuh untuk buah dan sayur. Lukis makanan kegemaran kamu dalam setiap bahagian.","Tip: Makan pelangi! Lobak merah yang jingga, kangkung yang hijau, tomato yang merah dan pisang yang kuning semuanya membantu badan.","Awas: Minuman manis dan gula-gula ialah makanan sekali-sekala, bukan makanan harian. Air kosong ialah minuman terbaik. Fakta menarik: Lebih separuh badan kita ialah air."]],
"sc_plant": [["A plant has roots, a stem, leaves and often flowers. Each part has its own job to help the plant live and grow.","Roots hold the plant in the soil and drink water. We eat some roots, like the cassava called ubi kayu. The stem carries water up to the leaves.","Leaves catch sunlight and make food for the plant. We eat bayam leaves. The flower makes fruit and seeds. A chilli is a fruit that grew from a flower.","Try it: Pull up a small weed or look at a pot plant. Point to its roots, stem, leaves and flower. Draw it and label the parts.","Tip: Roots are low, the stem is the straw, leaves are the kitchen and the flower makes the seeds.","Fun fact: Sugar cane is a stem that is full of sweet juice. Careful: The parts you eat are different in every plant."],["Tumbuhan ada akar, batang, daun dan selalunya bunga. Setiap bahagian ada tugasnya untuk membantu tumbuhan hidup dan membesar.","Akar memegang tumbuhan dalam tanah dan menyerap air. Kita makan sesetengah akar, seperti ubi kayu. Batang membawa air naik ke daun.","Daun menangkap cahaya matahari dan membuat makanan untuk tumbuhan. Kita makan daun bayam. Bunga menghasilkan buah dan biji. Cili ialah buah yang tumbuh daripada bunga.","Cuba ini: Cabut rumput kecil atau lihat pokok dalam pasu. Tunjuk akar, batang, daun dan bunganya. Lukis dan labelkan bahagiannya.","Tip: Akar di bawah, batang ialah penyedut minuman, daun ialah dapur dan bunga menghasilkan biji.","Fakta menarik: Tebu ialah batang yang penuh dengan air manis. Awas: Bahagian yang kita makan berbeza pada setiap tumbuhan."]],
"sc_weather": [["Weather tells us what the sky and air are like today. It can be sunny, cloudy, rainy, windy or stormy. It changes from hour to hour.","On a windy day, children fly a wau or a kite. On a rainy day we take an umbrella and wear shoes that can get wet.","In a thunderstorm, we see lightning first and hear thunder after. Light travels faster than sound. We stay inside until the storm is over.","Try it: Make a weather chart for 5 days. Look out of the window each morning and draw a sun, cloud, rain or wind symbol.","Tip: Look up, feel the air, then decide what to wear and what to do. Sunny means hat, rainy means umbrella.","Careful: A cloudy sky does not always mean rain. Fun fact: Dark, tall clouds are more likely to bring heavy rain."],["Cuaca memberitahu kita keadaan langit dan udara hari ini. Ia boleh cerah, mendung, hujan, berangin atau ribut. Ia berubah dari jam ke jam.","Pada hari berangin, kanak-kanak menerbangkan wau atau layang-layang. Pada hari hujan kita bawa payung dan pakai kasut yang boleh basah.","Semasa ribut petir, kita nampak kilat dahulu dan dengar guruh kemudian. Cahaya bergerak lebih laju daripada bunyi. Kita tinggal di dalam sehingga ribut reda.","Cuba ini: Buat carta cuaca selama 5 hari. Lihat ke luar tingkap setiap pagi dan lukis simbol matahari, awan, hujan atau angin.","Tip: Pandang ke atas, rasa udara, kemudian putuskan apa nak pakai dan apa nak buat. Cerah pakai topi, hujan bawa payung.","Awas: Langit mendung tidak selalu bermakna hujan. Fakta menarik: Awan tinggi yang gelap lebih mungkin membawa hujan lebat."]],
"sc_material": [["Things are made of materials such as wood, metal, glass, plastic, rubber, cloth and paper. We choose a material by how it feels and what it can do.","A spoon is metal because it is strong and does not break easily. A window is glass because we can see through it.","A raincoat is plastic because water cannot go through it. A towel is cloth because it soaks up water.","Try it: Find 6 things in the room. Say what each one is made of and why. Sort them into hard and soft, or see-through and not.","Tip: Ask two questions: what is it made of, and why is that a good choice? The use decides the material.","Fun fact: Rubber comes from the sap of rubber trees, and Malaysia makes many rubber gloves. Careful: A bottle can be glass or plastic!"],["Benda diperbuat daripada bahan seperti kayu, logam, kaca, plastik, getah, kain dan kertas. Kita memilih bahan mengikut rasanya dan kegunaannya.","Sudu diperbuat daripada logam kerana ia kuat dan tidak mudah patah. Tingkap diperbuat daripada kaca kerana kita boleh melihat menerusinya.","Baju hujan diperbuat daripada plastik kerana air tidak boleh menembusinya. Tuala diperbuat daripada kain kerana ia menyerap air.","Cuba ini: Cari 6 benda dalam bilik. Sebut ia diperbuat daripada apa dan kenapa. Asingkan kepada keras dan lembut, atau lutsinar dan tidak lutsinar.","Tip: Tanya dua soalan: diperbuat daripada apa, dan kenapa itu pilihan yang baik? Kegunaan menentukan bahan.","Fakta menarik: Getah datang daripada susu getah pokok getah, dan Malaysia membuat banyak sarung tangan getah. Awas: Botol boleh diperbuat daripada kaca atau plastik!"]],
"sc_magnet": [["A magnet is a special object that pulls some metals towards it. The pull is called magnetic force. It works even without touching.","A magnet picks up a paper clip and an iron nail. They stick to it. A magnet does not pick up a pencil, an eraser or a piece of paper.","A magnet has two ends called poles, north and south. Opposite poles pull together. The same poles push each other away.","Try it: Use a fridge magnet. Test 8 things and sort them into sticks and does not stick. Test through a sheet of paper too.","Tip: Opposites attract, likes repel. Remember that a magnet likes iron and steel.","Careful: Not all metals stick. Aluminium foil does not. Fun fact: Earth is like a giant magnet, and a compass needle points north."],["Magnet ialah benda istimewa yang menarik sesetengah logam ke arahnya. Tarikan itu dipanggil daya magnet. Ia berfungsi walaupun tanpa sentuhan.","Magnet mengangkat klip kertas dan paku besi. Benda itu melekat padanya. Magnet tidak mengangkat pensel, pemadam atau sehelai kertas.","Magnet ada dua hujung yang dipanggil kutub, utara dan selatan. Kutub yang berlawanan saling menarik. Kutub yang sama saling menolak.","Cuba ini: Guna magnet peti sejuk. Uji 8 benda dan asingkan kepada melekat dan tidak melekat. Uji juga melalui sehelai kertas.","Tip: Yang berlawanan menarik, yang sama menolak. Ingat bahawa magnet suka besi dan keluli.","Awas: Bukan semua logam melekat. Kerajang aluminium tidak melekat. Fakta menarik: Bumi seperti magnet gergasi dan jarum kompas menunjuk ke utara."]],
"sc_light": [["Light comes from a source like the Sun, a lamp or a torch. Light travels in straight lines. We see things when light bounces off them into our eyes.","A shadow forms when something blocks the light. If you stand in the sun, your body blocks the light and a dark shadow falls on the ground.","Glass is transparent, so light goes through it. Baking paper is translucent, so some light goes through. A wall is opaque, so no light goes through.","Try it: In a dark room, hold your hand in front of a torch against the wall. Move your hand closer to the torch. What happens to the shadow?","Tip: Block the light, make a shadow. A closer object makes a bigger shadow.","Fun fact: The Moon does not make its own light. It shines because the Sun shines on it. Careful: Never look straight at the Sun."],["Cahaya datang daripada punca seperti Matahari, lampu atau lampu suluh. Cahaya bergerak lurus. Kita nampak benda apabila cahaya terpantul daripadanya ke mata kita.","Bayang-bayang terbentuk apabila sesuatu menghalang cahaya. Jika kamu berdiri di bawah matahari, badan kamu menghalang cahaya dan bayang gelap jatuh ke tanah.","Kaca ialah lutsinar, jadi cahaya menembusinya. Kertas pembakar ialah lutsinar separa, jadi sedikit cahaya menembusinya. Dinding ialah legap, jadi tiada cahaya menembusinya.","Cuba ini: Dalam bilik gelap, letak tangan di hadapan lampu suluh ke arah dinding. Dekatkan tangan kepada lampu suluh. Apakah yang berlaku kepada bayang-bayang?","Tip: Halang cahaya, bayang terbentuk. Benda yang lebih dekat membuat bayang yang lebih besar.","Fakta menarik: Bulan tidak menghasilkan cahayanya sendiri. Ia bersinar kerana Matahari menyinarinya. Awas: Jangan sekali-kali tenung Matahari."]],
"sc_space": [["The Solar System is the Sun and everything that goes round it. The Sun is a star, a giant ball of hot, glowing gas. Eight planets travel round it.","In order from the Sun: Mercury, Venus, Earth, Mars, Jupiter, Saturn, Uranus and Neptune. In Malay: Utarid, Zuhrah, Bumi, Marikh, Musytari, Zuhal, Uranus, Neptun.","Jupiter is the biggest planet. Saturn has bright rings. Earth is the only planet we know that has life, with water and air for us.","Try it: Use 8 fruits or balls of different sizes. Line them up in order from a lamp that stands for the Sun. Say the names out loud.","Tip: My Very Easy Method Just Speeds Up Naming: Mercury, Venus, Earth, Mars, Jupiter, Saturn, Uranus, Neptune.","Fun fact: Earth takes one year to go round the Sun. Malaysia sent Sheikh Muszaphar Shukor into space in 2007. Careful: The Sun is a star, not a planet."],["Sistem Suria ialah Matahari dan semua yang mengelilinginya. Matahari ialah bintang, bola gas panas yang bercahaya dan sangat besar. Lapan planet mengelilinginya.","Mengikut susunan dari Matahari: Utarid, Zuhrah, Bumi, Marikh, Musytari, Zuhal, Uranus dan Neptun. Dalam bahasa Inggeris: Mercury, Venus, Earth, Mars, Jupiter, Saturn, Uranus, Neptune.","Musytari ialah planet paling besar. Zuhal ada cincin yang terang. Bumi ialah satu-satunya planet yang kita tahu ada hidupan, dengan air dan udara untuk kita.","Cuba ini: Guna 8 biji buah atau bola yang berlainan saiz. Susun mengikut turutan dari sebuah lampu yang mewakili Matahari. Sebut nama-namanya dengan kuat.","Tip: Sebut nama planet dari yang paling dekat dengan Matahari hingga yang paling jauh, berulang-ulang seperti lagu.","Fakta menarik: Bumi mengambil masa setahun untuk mengelilingi Matahari. Malaysia menghantar Sheikh Muszaphar Shukor ke angkasa pada 2007. Awas: Matahari ialah bintang, bukan planet."]],
"sc_energy": [["Energy is what makes things move, light up, warm up and make sound. Without energy, nothing can happen. We cannot see it, but we see what it does.","Our energy comes from food. Rice gives you energy to run and play. A torch gets energy from its battery. A solar panel gets energy from the Sun.","Energy can change its form. A fan changes electricity into moving air. A bulb changes electricity into light and a little heat.","Try it: Rub your hands together fast for 10 seconds. Feel them get warm. Your moving energy turned into heat energy!","Tip: Energy has many forms: light, heat, sound and movement. Ask, where did it come from and what did it turn into?","Fun fact: The light of the Sun takes about 8 minutes to reach Earth. Careful: Energy changes form, so turn off lights to save electricity."],["Tenaga ialah sesuatu yang membuat benda bergerak, menyala, menjadi panas dan mengeluarkan bunyi. Tanpa tenaga, tiada apa yang boleh berlaku. Kita tidak nampak tenaga, tetapi kita nampak kesannya.","Tenaga kita datang daripada makanan. Nasi memberi kamu tenaga untuk berlari dan bermain. Lampu suluh mendapat tenaga daripada bateri. Panel solar mendapat tenaga daripada Matahari.","Tenaga boleh bertukar bentuk. Kipas menukar elektrik kepada udara yang bergerak. Mentol menukar elektrik kepada cahaya dan sedikit haba.","Cuba ini: Gosok kedua-dua tangan dengan laju selama 10 saat. Rasa tangan menjadi hangat. Tenaga gerakan kamu bertukar menjadi tenaga haba!","Tip: Tenaga ada banyak bentuk: cahaya, haba, bunyi dan gerakan. Tanya, dari mana datangnya dan menjadi apa?","Fakta menarik: Cahaya Matahari mengambil masa kira-kira 8 minit untuk sampai ke Bumi. Awas: Tenaga bertukar bentuk, jadi tutup lampu untuk jimat elektrik."]],
"sc_larut": [["Some things mix into water and seem to disappear. This is called dissolving. The water with the dissolved thing is called a solution.","Stir a spoon of salt into a glass of water. The salt goes away, but the water tastes salty. The salt is still there, too small to see.","Sand does not dissolve. It sinks and stays at the bottom. Cooking oil does not dissolve either. It floats on top of the water.","Try it: Test sugar, salt, sand and rice in 4 clear cups of water. Stir each one. Which ones dissolve? Which do not?","Tip: Stir and warm water make things dissolve faster. Dissolve means it mixes in and you cannot see it.","Fun fact: Sea water tastes salty because salt has dissolved in it. Careful: Never taste science experiments without asking an adult."],["Sesetengah benda bercampur dalam air dan seperti hilang. Ini dipanggil melarut. Air yang mengandungi benda terlarut dipanggil larutan.","Kacau satu sudu garam dalam segelas air. Garam itu hilang, tetapi air terasa masin. Garam masih ada, terlalu kecil untuk dilihat.","Pasir tidak larut. Ia tenggelam dan tinggal di dasar. Minyak masak juga tidak larut. Ia terapung di atas air.","Cuba ini: Uji gula, garam, pasir dan beras dalam 4 cawan jernih berisi air. Kacau setiap satu. Yang mana larut? Yang mana tidak?","Tip: Kacau dan air suam membuat benda melarut lebih cepat. Melarut bermaksud bercampur dan tidak nampak lagi.","Fakta menarik: Air laut masin kerana garam telah larut di dalamnya. Awas: Jangan rasa eksperimen sains tanpa bertanya orang dewasa."]],
"sc_apung": [["Some things float on water and some things sink to the bottom. A floating thing stays on top. A sinking thing goes down.","A wooden spoon, a cork and an empty plastic bottle float. A stone, a key and a metal spoon sink.","Size does not decide it. A tiny pebble sinks, but a huge wooden log floats. It depends on the material and its shape.","Try it: Make a clay ball and drop it in water. It sinks. Now shape the clay like a boat with high sides. Does it float?","Tip: Guess first, then test. Scientists always predict and then check.","Fun fact: Big ships are made of steel but they float, because their shape holds a lot of air. Careful: Do the test with a grown-up near water."],["Ada benda yang timbul di atas air dan ada benda yang tenggelam ke dasar. Benda yang timbul kekal di atas. Benda yang tenggelam turun ke bawah.","Sudu kayu, gabus dan botol plastik kosong timbul. Batu, kunci dan sudu logam tenggelam.","Saiz tidak menentukannya. Batu kecil tenggelam, tetapi kayu balak yang besar timbul. Ia bergantung pada bahan dan bentuknya.","Cuba ini: Buat bola tanah liat dan jatuhkan dalam air. Ia tenggelam. Sekarang bentuk tanah liat seperti bot dengan sisi yang tinggi. Adakah ia timbul?","Tip: Teka dahulu, kemudian uji. Ahli sains sentiasa meramal kemudian menyemak.","Fakta menarik: Kapal besar diperbuat daripada keluli tetapi ia timbul, kerana bentuknya memerangkap banyak udara. Awas: Buat ujian dengan orang dewasa berdekatan air."]],
"sc_digital": [["Digital devices are machines like phones, tablets, computers, TVs and cameras. They help us talk, learn, play and take pictures.","You can video call grandma on a phone and see her face. You can play a learning game on a tablet. A camera keeps a memory of your birthday party.","Use devices safely. Ask a grown-up first, and use them where a grown-up can see. Keep your name, address and passwords secret.","Try it: Count the digital devices in your home. Which ones help you learn? Which ones help the family talk to each other?","Tip: Stop, ask, then tap. If something online feels scary or strange, close it and tell a grown-up.","Fun fact: The first computers were as big as a room. Careful: Rest your eyes. Look far away often and play outside too."],["Peranti digital ialah mesin seperti telefon, tablet, komputer, TV dan kamera. Ia membantu kita bercakap, belajar, bermain dan mengambil gambar.","Kamu boleh membuat panggilan video dengan nenek dan melihat wajahnya. Kamu boleh bermain permainan pembelajaran di tablet. Kamera menyimpan kenangan majlis hari jadi kamu.","Guna peranti dengan selamat. Minta izin orang dewasa dahulu dan guna di tempat yang orang dewasa boleh nampak. Rahsiakan nama, alamat dan kata laluan kamu.","Cuba ini: Kira peranti digital di rumah kamu. Yang mana membantu kamu belajar? Yang mana membantu keluarga berbual?","Tip: Berhenti, tanya, kemudian sentuh. Jika sesuatu dalam talian terasa menakutkan atau pelik, tutup dan beritahu orang dewasa.","Fakta menarik: Komputer pertama sebesar sebuah bilik. Awas: Rehatkan mata. Kerap pandang jauh dan bermainlah di luar juga."]],
"sc2_homes": [["Animals need a safe place to rest, hide from danger and raise their babies. This place is called a home.","A bird builds a nest in a tree. A bee lives in a hive with many other bees. A fish lives in water.","A rabbit digs a burrow under the ground. Ants live in an anthill made of tiny bits of soil. A cow stays in a shed on a farm.","Try it: Draw 3 animals and their homes. Then ask a friend to match each animal to the right home.","Tip: The home fits the animal. Fish need water, birds need trees, and rabbits need soft ground to dig.","Fun fact: A honeybee hive can hold thousands of bees, all working together like a tiny town!"],["Haiwan memerlukan tempat selamat untuk berehat, bersembunyi daripada bahaya dan membesarkan anak. Tempat ini dipanggil rumah.","Burung membina sarang di atas pokok. Lebah tinggal di dalam sarang bersama banyak lebah lain. Ikan tinggal di dalam air.","Arnab menggali lubang di bawah tanah. Semut tinggal di busut kecil daripada tanah. Lembu tinggal di kandang di ladang.","Cuba ini: Lukis 3 haiwan dan rumah mereka. Kemudian minta kawan memadankan setiap haiwan dengan rumah yang betul.","Tip: Rumah sesuai dengan haiwan. Ikan perlukan air, burung perlukan pokok, dan arnab perlukan tanah lembut untuk digali.","Fakta menarik: Satu sarang lebah madu boleh memuatkan beribu-ribu ekor lebah yang bekerja bersama seperti bandar kecil!"]],
"sc2_germs": [["Germs are tiny living things too small to see. Some can make us sick, so we keep our hands clean.","Wash hands with soap and water before eating and after using the toilet. Rub the front, back and between fingers.","When you cough or sneeze, cover your mouth with your elbow or a tissue. This stops germs from flying to others.","Try it: Sing Happy Birthday twice while you scrub with soap. That takes about 20 seconds, just right for clean hands.","Tip: Soap, scrub, rinse, dry. Four steps, and the germs wash down the drain.","Fun fact: Soap does not kill germs only. It lifts them off your skin so the water can wash them away."],["Kuman ialah makhluk hidup yang sangat kecil dan tidak dapat dilihat. Ada yang boleh menyebabkan kita sakit, jadi kita menjaga tangan kita bersih.","Cuci tangan dengan sabun dan air sebelum makan dan selepas ke tandas. Gosok bahagian depan, belakang dan celah jari.","Apabila batuk atau bersin, tutup mulut dengan lengan atau tisu. Ini menghalang kuman terbang kepada orang lain.","Cuba ini: Nyanyi lagu Selamat Hari Jadi dua kali sambil menggosok dengan sabun. Ia mengambil kira-kira 20 saat, sesuai untuk tangan bersih.","Tip: Sabun, gosok, bilas, lap. Empat langkah, dan kuman hanyut ke dalam longkang.","Fakta menarik: Sabun bukan sahaja membunuh kuman. Ia mengangkat kuman dari kulit supaya air dapat membasuhnya."]],
"sc2_living": [["Living things grow, eat or take in food, breathe, make babies and can die. Non-living things do none of these.","A cat is living: it eats, grows and has kittens. A tree is living too, even though it does not walk about.","A toy car, a rock and a spoon are non-living. They do not grow or need food, even if they move when pushed.","Try it: Go around the room and sort 6 things into two groups: living and non-living. Explain why for each one.","Tip: Ask, does it grow and need food? If yes, it is living. If no, it is non-living.","Careful: Fire and clouds seem to move and grow, but they are not alive. They do not eat, breathe or have babies."],["Benda hidup membesar, makan, bernafas, membiak dan boleh mati. Benda bukan hidup tidak melakukan semua ini.","Kucing ialah benda hidup: ia makan, membesar dan ada anak kucing. Pokok juga hidup, walaupun ia tidak berjalan.","Kereta mainan, batu dan sudu ialah benda bukan hidup. Ia tidak membesar atau perlukan makanan, walaupun bergerak apabila ditolak.","Cuba ini: Pergi sekeliling bilik dan asingkan 6 benda kepada dua kumpulan: hidup dan bukan hidup. Terangkan sebabnya.","Tip: Tanya, adakah ia membesar dan perlukan makanan? Jika ya, ia hidup. Jika tidak, ia bukan hidup.","Berhati-hati: Api dan awan nampak bergerak dan membesar, tetapi tidak hidup. Ia tidak makan, bernafas atau beranak."]],
"sc2_eats": [["Animals eat different foods. Plant eaters eat only plants. Meat eaters eat other animals. Some animals eat both.","A cow and an elephant eat plants like grass and leaves. A tiger eats meat, such as deer and wild boar.","A chicken eats seeds and small insects, so it eats both plants and animals. People eat both too!","Try it: Make three columns: plants, meat and both. Put 6 animals in the right column, such as goat, eagle and duck.","Tip: Plant eaters are called herbivores, meat eaters are carnivores, and eaters of both are omnivores.","Careful: Big does not always mean meat eater. An elephant is huge but eats only plants!"],["Haiwan makan makanan yang berbeza. Herbivor makan tumbuhan sahaja. Karnivor makan haiwan lain. Ada haiwan yang makan kedua-duanya.","Lembu dan gajah makan tumbuhan seperti rumput dan daun. Harimau makan daging, seperti rusa dan babi hutan.","Ayam makan biji-bijian dan serangga kecil, jadi ia makan tumbuhan dan haiwan. Manusia juga makan kedua-duanya!","Cuba ini: Buat tiga lajur: tumbuhan, daging dan kedua-duanya. Letak 6 haiwan dalam lajur yang betul, seperti kambing, helang dan itik.","Tip: Pemakan tumbuhan ialah herbivor, pemakan daging ialah karnivor, dan pemakan kedua-duanya ialah omnivor.","Berhati-hati: Besar tidak selalu bermaksud pemakan daging. Gajah sangat besar tetapi hanya makan tumbuhan!"]],
"sc2_insects": [["An insect is a small animal with 6 legs, 3 body parts (head, chest and tummy) and 2 feelers called antennae.","An ant has 6 legs and 2 antennae, so it is an insect. A butterfly has 6 legs, 2 antennae and 4 wings. It is also an insect.","A beetle, a dragonfly and a bee are insects too. Many insects can fly, but not all of them can.","Try it: Look outside for 3 small creatures. Count the legs on each one. Six legs? Then it is an insect.","Tip: Six legs, three parts, two feelers. Say it like a chant: 6, 3, 2!","Fun fact: A spider has 8 legs, so it is not an insect. And butterflies taste things with their feet!"],["Serangga ialah haiwan kecil dengan 6 kaki, 3 bahagian badan (kepala, dada dan perut) dan 2 sesungut.","Semut ada 6 kaki dan 2 sesungut, jadi ia serangga. Rama-rama ada 6 kaki, 2 sesungut dan 4 sayap. Ia juga serangga.","Kumbang, pepatung dan lebah juga serangga. Banyak serangga boleh terbang, tetapi tidak semua.","Cuba ini: Cari 3 makhluk kecil di luar. Kira kaki pada setiap satu. Enam kaki? Maka ia serangga.","Tip: Enam kaki, tiga bahagian, dua sesungut. Sebut seperti cogan kata: 6, 3, 2!","Fakta menarik: Labah-labah ada 8 kaki, jadi ia bukan serangga. Dan rama-rama merasa makanan dengan kakinya!"]],
"sc2_wildlife": [["Malaysia has rainforests and seas full of special animals. We must protect them so they have a safe home.","The orang utan lives in the forests of Borneo. Its name means person of the forest in Malay, and it eats mostly fruit.","The harimau Malaya, or Malayan tiger, lives in the forests of Peninsular Malaysia. It is on our national coat of arms, and it is endangered.","A penyu, or sea turtle, comes out of the sea to lay eggs on the beach. The tiny baby turtles then crawl to the sea at night.","Try it: Draw one of these animals and write one way to help it, such as not leaving rubbish on the beach.","Tip: Remember O, H and P: orang utan in Borneo forests, harimau in the peninsula, penyu on beaches."],["Malaysia ada hutan hujan dan laut yang penuh dengan haiwan istimewa. Kita mesti melindungi mereka supaya mereka ada rumah yang selamat.","Orang utan tinggal di hutan Borneo. Namanya bermaksud orang hutan dan ia makan buah-buahan sebagai makanan utama.","Harimau Malaya tinggal di hutan Semenanjung Malaysia. Ia terdapat pada jata negara kita, dan ia terancam.","Penyu keluar dari laut untuk bertelur di pantai. Anak penyu yang kecil kemudian merangkak ke laut pada waktu malam.","Cuba ini: Lukis salah satu haiwan ini dan tulis satu cara membantunya, seperti tidak membuang sampah di pantai.","Tip: Ingat O, H dan P: orang utan di hutan Borneo, harimau di semenanjung, penyu di pantai."]],
"sc2_weathermy": [["Malaysia is warm all year. It does not have snow, but it has wet times with lots of rain and drier times with less rain.","Heavy rain often comes during the monsoon, which is a season of strong winds and rain. Many places get more rain from about November to March.","On wet days we use an umbrella and wear a raincoat. On dry hot days we wear a hat, drink water and stay in the shade.","Try it: Put a clear cup outside on a rainy day. After the rain, see how much water collected. This shows how much rain fell.","Tip: Wet days need an umbrella, dry days need a hat and water. Look at the sky before you go out!","Careful: Even in the dry season it may still rain sometimes. Always check the weather before you play outside."],["Malaysia panas sepanjang tahun. Ia tidak ada salji, tetapi ada masa basah dengan banyak hujan dan masa yang lebih kering dengan kurang hujan.","Hujan lebat selalu datang semasa monsun, iaitu musim angin kuat dan hujan. Banyak tempat menerima lebih hujan dari kira-kira November hingga Mac.","Pada hari hujan kita guna payung dan pakai baju hujan. Pada hari panas dan kering kita pakai topi, minum air dan berteduh.","Cuba ini: Letak cawan jernih di luar pada hari hujan. Selepas hujan, lihat berapa banyak air terkumpul. Ini menunjukkan berapa banyak hujan turun.","Tip: Hari basah perlukan payung, hari kering perlukan topi dan air. Lihat langit sebelum keluar!","Berhati-hati: Walaupun pada musim kering, hujan masih boleh turun kadang-kadang. Semak cuaca sebelum bermain di luar."]],
"sc2_seeds": [["A seed holds a tiny baby plant inside. When it gets water, warmth and air, it wakes up and starts to grow. This is called germination.","First a small root grows down into the soil. Then a shoot grows up toward the light and opens its first leaves.","A bean seed can sprout in just a few days. Rice, corn and sunflower seeds grow in the same way.","Try it: Put a bean on wet tissue in a clear cup. Keep it damp and warm. Look every day and draw what you see.","Tip: Root goes down, shoot goes up. Seeds begin with water, then the plant needs light later.","Fun fact: A seed does not need sunlight to start growing. It uses the food stored inside the seed first."],["Biji benih menyimpan tumbuhan bayi yang kecil di dalamnya. Apabila mendapat air, kehangatan dan udara, ia bangun dan mula tumbuh. Ini dipanggil percambahan.","Mula-mula akar kecil tumbuh ke bawah ke dalam tanah. Kemudian pucuk tumbuh ke atas menuju cahaya dan membuka daun pertamanya.","Biji kacang boleh bertunas dalam beberapa hari sahaja. Padi, jagung dan biji bunga matahari tumbuh dengan cara yang sama.","Cuba ini: Letak sebiji kacang di atas tisu basah dalam cawan jernih. Pastikan lembap dan hangat. Lihat setiap hari dan lukis apa yang kamu nampak.","Tip: Akar ke bawah, pucuk ke atas. Biji bermula dengan air, tumbuhan perlukan cahaya kemudian.","Fakta menarik: Biji benih tidak perlukan cahaya matahari untuk mula tumbuh. Ia menggunakan makanan yang tersimpan dalam biji dahulu."]],
"sc2_fruits": [["Most fruits have an outside skin, soft flesh we eat, and seeds inside. The seeds can grow into new trees.","The durian is called the king of fruits. It has a thorny husk, creamy flesh and big seeds, and it has a very strong smell.","The rambutan has a red hairy skin. Inside is white juicy flesh and one seed. Its name comes from the Malay word rambut, which means hair.","Try it: Share a fruit with a grown-up. Name its skin, flesh and seeds. Then plant a seed in a pot and water it.","Tip: Skin, flesh, seed. Every fruit has these three parts, even if the shapes look different.","Fun fact: A tomato and a cucumber hold seeds, so they are fruits too, even though we eat them in meals."],["Kebanyakan buah ada kulit di luar, isi lembut yang kita makan, dan biji di dalam. Biji boleh tumbuh menjadi pokok baharu.","Durian dipanggil raja buah-buahan. Ia ada kulit berduri, isi berkrim dan biji besar, dan baunya sangat kuat.","Rambutan ada kulit merah berbulu. Di dalamnya ada isi putih berair dan satu biji. Namanya datang daripada perkataan rambut.","Cuba ini: Kongsi sebiji buah dengan orang dewasa. Namakan kulit, isi dan bijinya. Kemudian tanam satu biji dalam pasu dan siram.","Tip: Kulit, isi, biji. Setiap buah ada tiga bahagian ini, walaupun bentuknya berbeza.","Fakta menarik: Tomato dan timun mengandungi biji, jadi ia juga buah, walaupun kita makan dalam hidangan."]],
"sc2_hotcold": [["Hot and cold tell us how much heat something has. We can feel them, but a thermometer measures them with a number.","Hot tea feels hot and ice cream feels cold. Water freezes at 0 degrees Celsius and boils at 100 degrees Celsius.","Our body is about 37 degrees Celsius. A warm day in Malaysia is often about 30 degrees Celsius.","Try it: Put your hand near a cup of warm water, then a cup of cool water. Tell a grown-up which is hotter.","Tip: Never touch hot things like a kettle or stove. Use a thermometer or ask a grown-up.","Careful: Our hands can be tricked. A metal spoon may feel colder than a wooden one, even in the same room."],["Panas dan sejuk memberitahu berapa banyak haba yang ada pada sesuatu. Kita boleh merasainya, tetapi termometer mengukurnya dengan nombor.","Teh panas rasa panas dan aiskrim rasa sejuk. Air membeku pada 0 darjah Celsius dan mendidih pada 100 darjah Celsius.","Badan kita kira-kira 37 darjah Celsius. Hari panas di Malaysia selalunya kira-kira 30 darjah Celsius.","Cuba ini: Letak tangan berhampiran secawan air suam, kemudian secawan air sejuk. Beritahu orang dewasa yang mana lebih panas.","Tip: Jangan sentuh benda panas seperti cerek atau dapur. Guna termometer atau minta orang dewasa.","Berhati-hati: Tangan kita boleh tertipu. Sudu logam mungkin terasa lebih sejuk daripada sudu kayu, walaupun dalam bilik yang sama."]],
"sc2_sound": [["Sound is made when something vibrates, which means it shakes back and forth very fast. We hear the shaking through the air.","Pluck a stretched rubber band and watch it blur. That shaking makes the sound. When it stops shaking, the sound stops too.","Put your fingers on your throat and hum. You can feel the vibration. A big drum makes a low sound and a small drum makes a high sound.","Try it: Put a little rice on a stretched plastic sheet over a bowl. Clap loudly near it and watch the rice jump.","Tip: Sound needs shaking. No shaking, no sound. Touch it and feel it.","Fun fact: Sound travels through air, so in space, where there is no air, no one can hear a sound."],["Bunyi terhasil apabila sesuatu bergetar, iaitu bergoyang ke depan dan ke belakang dengan sangat laju. Kita mendengar goyangan itu melalui udara.","Petik gelang getah yang diregang dan lihat ia kabur. Goyangan itu menghasilkan bunyi. Apabila ia berhenti bergoyang, bunyi juga berhenti.","Letak jari di leher dan bersenandung. Kamu boleh rasa getarannya. Gendang besar menghasilkan bunyi rendah dan gendang kecil menghasilkan bunyi tinggi.","Cuba ini: Letak sedikit beras di atas plastik yang diregang di atas mangkuk. Tepuk tangan kuat berhampiran dan lihat beras melompat.","Tip: Bunyi perlukan goyangan. Tiada goyangan, tiada bunyi. Sentuh dan rasailah.","Fakta menarik: Bunyi bergerak melalui udara, jadi di angkasa lepas, yang tiada udara, tiada siapa dapat mendengar bunyi."]],
"sc2_recycle": [["The 3Rs help keep our Earth clean. Reduce means use less. Reuse means use again. Recycle means turn old things into new ones.","Reduce: bring your own bottle instead of buying a new plastic one. Reuse: use an old jam jar as a pencil holder.","Recycle: put paper, plastic, cans and glass in the right bins so factories can make new things from them. Paper goes in the blue bin.","Try it: Find 3 things in your bin that could be reused or recycled. Draw how you could use them again.","Tip: Think R, R, R: use less, use again, make anew. Rubbish is the last choice.","Fun fact: Recycling saves trees, because used paper can be made into new paper."],["3R membantu memastikan Bumi kita bersih. Kurangkan bermaksud guna kurang. Guna semula bermaksud guna lagi. Kitar semula bermaksud menukar barang lama menjadi barang baharu.","Kurangkan: bawa botol sendiri dan jangan beli botol plastik baharu. Guna semula: guna balang jem lama sebagai bekas pensel.","Kitar semula: letak kertas, plastik, tin dan kaca dalam tong yang betul supaya kilang boleh membuat barang baharu. Kertas masuk tong biru.","Cuba ini: Cari 3 benda dalam tong sampah yang boleh digunakan semula atau dikitar semula. Lukis cara kamu menggunakannya lagi.","Tip: Fikir R, R, R: guna kurang, guna lagi, buat baharu. Sampah ialah pilihan terakhir.","Fakta menarik: Kitar semula menjimatkan pokok, kerana kertas lama boleh dibuat menjadi kertas baharu."]],
"sc2_sleepmove": [["Our bodies need sleep to rest and grow, and exercise to stay strong. Both help us feel good and think well.","Children need about 10 hours of sleep at night. Go to bed at the same time every night, and your body gets used to it.","Children should move and play for about 1 hour every day. Run, skip, jump, swim or ride a bicycle.","Try it: Do 10 jumping jacks, then 10 slow breaths. Feel your heart beat fast, then slow down again.","Tip: Move in the day, rest at night. Turn off screens before bed so you can fall asleep easily.","Fun fact: While you sleep, your body still works. Your heart beats and your lungs breathe all night."],["Badan kita perlukan tidur untuk berehat dan membesar, dan senaman untuk kekal kuat. Kedua-duanya membantu kita rasa sihat dan berfikir dengan baik.","Kanak-kanak perlukan kira-kira 10 jam tidur pada waktu malam. Tidur pada waktu yang sama setiap malam, dan badan kamu akan biasa.","Kanak-kanak perlu bergerak dan bermain kira-kira 1 jam setiap hari. Berlari, melompat tali, melompat, berenang atau berbasikal.","Cuba ini: Buat 10 lompat bintang, kemudian 10 nafas perlahan. Rasa jantung berdegup laju, kemudian perlahan semula.","Tip: Bergerak waktu siang, berehat waktu malam. Matikan skrin sebelum tidur supaya mudah lena.","Fakta menarik: Semasa kamu tidur, badan masih bekerja. Jantung berdegup dan paru-paru bernafas sepanjang malam."]],
"sc2_moon": [["The Moon seems to change shape each night. These shapes are called phases. We see different amounts of its sunlit side.","The new moon looks dark. Then a thin crescent appears, then a half moon, and then a full moon that looks like a bright circle.","The Moon does not make its own light. It shines because it reflects light from the Sun. The cycle takes about one month.","Try it: Look at the Moon for a week and draw its shape each night. Write the date beside every drawing.","Tip: Thin crescent, half, full, then it shrinks again. Think grow, grow, glow, go.","Fun fact: Many Muslims watch for the thin crescent moon to know when a new month, such as Syawal for Hari Raya, begins."],["Bulan nampak berubah bentuk setiap malam. Bentuk-bentuk ini dipanggil fasa. Kita melihat bahagian yang berbeza daripada sisinya yang disinari matahari.","Bulan baharu nampak gelap. Kemudian bulan sabit nipis muncul, kemudian bulan separuh, dan kemudian bulan purnama yang nampak seperti bulatan terang.","Bulan tidak menghasilkan cahayanya sendiri. Ia bersinar kerana memantulkan cahaya Matahari. Satu kitaran mengambil kira-kira satu bulan.","Cuba ini: Lihat Bulan selama seminggu dan lukis bentuknya setiap malam. Tulis tarikh di sebelah setiap lukisan.","Tip: Sabit nipis, separuh, purnama, kemudian mengecil semula. Ingat: membesar, membesar, bersinar, mengecil.","Fakta menarik: Ramai orang Islam melihat anak bulan sabit untuk mengetahui bila bulan baharu, seperti Syawal untuk Hari Raya, bermula."]],
"sc2_friction": [["Friction is a force that happens when two things rub against each other. It slows things down or stops them from sliding.","A toy car rolls far on a smooth tile floor but stops quickly on a rough carpet. The carpet has more friction.","Wheels roll more easily than flat things slide, so a trolley is easy to push. Shoe soles have grooves so we do not slip.","Try it: Push a toy car on tile, carpet and a towel. Which goes furthest? Which stops fastest? Write what you find.","Tip: Rough means more friction, smooth means less friction. Rough grips, smooth glides.","Fun fact: Rub your hands together fast. They feel warm because of friction!"],["Geseran ialah daya yang berlaku apabila dua benda bergesel antara satu sama lain. Ia memperlahankan benda atau menghalangnya daripada meluncur.","Kereta mainan bergerak jauh di atas lantai jubin yang licin tetapi berhenti cepat di atas permaidani yang kasar. Permaidani ada lebih geseran.","Roda bergolek lebih mudah daripada benda rata yang meluncur, jadi troli mudah ditolak. Tapak kasut ada alur supaya kita tidak tergelincir.","Cuba ini: Tolak kereta mainan di atas jubin, permaidani dan tuala. Yang mana paling jauh? Yang mana berhenti paling cepat? Tulis hasilnya.","Tip: Kasar bermaksud lebih geseran, licin bermaksud kurang geseran. Kasar mencengkam, licin meluncur.","Fakta menarik: Gosok tangan dengan laju. Ia terasa hangat kerana geseran!"]],
"sc2_elec": [["Electricity makes lights, fans and TVs work. It is very useful, but it can hurt us if we are not careful. We must follow the safety rules.","Never put fingers or objects into a socket. Always ask a grown-up to plug and unplug things for you.","Keep water away from electrical things. Water and electricity are a dangerous mix, so dry your hands first.","Try it: Walk around your home with a grown-up and spot 5 safe electrical things. Point out any wires that look worn or broken.","Tip: Look, do not touch. Tell a grown-up if something looks broken. Pull the plug, not the wire.","Good to know: If there is an emergency, ask a grown-up to call 999 in Malaysia. Staying calm helps."],["Elektrik menjadikan lampu, kipas dan televisyen berfungsi. Ia berguna, tetapi boleh mencederakan kita jika kita tidak berhati-hati. Ikut peraturan keselamatan.","Jangan sekali-kali masukkan jari atau benda ke dalam soket. Sentiasa minta orang dewasa mencucuk dan mencabut palam untuk kamu.","Jauhkan air daripada barang elektrik. Air dan elektrik adalah gabungan yang berbahaya, jadi keringkan tangan dahulu.","Cuba ini: Berjalan di rumah bersama orang dewasa dan cari 5 barang elektrik yang selamat. Tunjuk wayar yang nampak lusuh atau rosak.","Tip: Lihat, jangan sentuh. Beritahu orang dewasa jika sesuatu nampak rosak. Tarik palam, bukan wayar.","Baik diketahui: Jika ada kecemasan, minta orang dewasa menelefon 999 di Malaysia. Bertenang membantu."]],
"sc2_air": [["Air is all around us, even though we cannot see it. It fills space, can move and can push on things.","Blow up a balloon. It gets bigger because air fills it. Feel the wind on your face. Wind is air that is moving.","An empty cup is really full of air. Push a cup upside down into a bowl of water, and air inside keeps some water out.","Try it: Wave a paper fan in front of your face. You can feel the air move even though you cannot see it.","Tip: Air is invisible, but you can feel it, hear it in the wind and see what it moves, like leaves and kites.","Fun fact: Air is needed for all living things to breathe. Birds, fish, people and trees all use it."],["Udara ada di sekeliling kita, walaupun kita tidak dapat melihatnya. Ia memenuhi ruang, boleh bergerak dan boleh menolak benda.","Tiup belon. Ia membesar kerana udara memenuhinya. Rasa angin di muka. Angin ialah udara yang bergerak.","Cawan kosong sebenarnya penuh dengan udara. Tolak cawan terbalik ke dalam mangkuk air, dan udara di dalamnya menghalang sebahagian air masuk.","Cuba ini: Kipas kertas di hadapan muka. Kamu boleh rasa udara bergerak walaupun tidak nampak.","Tip: Udara tidak nampak, tetapi kamu boleh merasa, mendengarnya dalam angin dan melihat apa yang digerakkan, seperti daun dan layang-layang.","Fakta menarik: Semua benda hidup perlukan udara untuk bernafas. Burung, ikan, manusia dan pokok semuanya menggunakannya."]],
"sc2_vertebrates": [["Animals with backbones can be sorted into groups by their bodies. Four big groups are mammals, birds, reptiles and fish.","Mammals have fur or hair and feed their babies milk. Birds have feathers, wings and a beak, and they lay eggs.","Reptiles have dry scales, and most lay eggs. Fish have scales and fins and breathe in water with gills.","Try it: Sort a cat, hen, crocodile, shark, whale and snake into the four groups. Say why for each one.","Tip: Fur, feathers, scales, gills. Match the body cover to the group!","Careful: A whale lives in the sea but breathes air and feeds milk, so it is a mammal, not a fish. A bat is a mammal too!"],["Haiwan bertulang belakang boleh dikumpulkan mengikut badan mereka. Empat kumpulan besar ialah mamalia, burung, reptilia dan ikan.","Mamalia ada bulu dan menyusukan anak. Burung ada bulu pelepah, sayap dan paruh, dan bertelur.","Reptilia ada sisik kering, dan kebanyakannya bertelur. Ikan ada sisik dan sirip dan bernafas dalam air dengan insang.","Cuba ini: Asingkan kucing, ayam betina, buaya, jerung, ikan paus dan ular kepada empat kumpulan. Beri sebab untuk setiap satu.","Tip: Bulu, bulu pelepah, sisik, insang. Padankan penutup badan dengan kumpulannya!","Berhati-hati: Ikan paus tinggal di laut tetapi bernafas dengan udara dan menyusukan anak, jadi ia mamalia, bukan ikan. Kelawar juga mamalia!"]],
"s_cause": [["A cause is why something happens. An effect is what happens because of it. We can say: this happened because of that.","Ice lolly in the hot sun is the cause. It melts and drips. That is the effect. No sun, no melting, so the sun was the cause.","A glass slips from a wet hand. It falls and breaks. The slip is the cause and the broken glass is the effect.","Try the activity below. Tap one cause button and watch what happens. Then say it with because: it happened because of the cause.","Try it: Ask, what happened? Then ask, why? Find 3 cause-and-effect pairs on your way to school today.","Careful: The cause comes first and the effect comes after. Fun fact: Scientists look for causes to understand how the world works."],["Sebab ialah mengapa sesuatu berlaku. Akibat ialah apa yang berlaku kerananya. Kita boleh kata: ini berlaku kerana itu.","Aiskrim batang di bawah matahari panas ialah sebab. Ia cair dan menitis. Itu akibatnya. Tiada matahari, tiada cair, jadi matahari ialah sebab.","Sebiji gelas tergelincir daripada tangan yang basah. Ia jatuh dan pecah. Tergelincir ialah sebab dan gelas pecah ialah akibat.","Cuba aktiviti di bawah. Tekan satu butang sebab dan lihat apa yang berlaku. Kemudian sebut dengan kerana: ia berlaku kerana sebab itu.","Cuba ini: Tanya, apa yang berlaku? Kemudian tanya, mengapa? Cari 3 pasangan sebab dan akibat dalam perjalanan ke sekolah hari ini.","Awas: Sebab datang dahulu dan akibat datang kemudian. Fakta menarik: Ahli sains mencari sebab untuk memahami cara dunia berfungsi."]],
"s_plants": [["Plants are living things, so they need things to grow. Plants need sunlight, water, air and soil. Without them they get weak and may die.","A potted plant by the window gets sunlight and grows green and tall. A plant forgotten for many days in a dark cupboard turns yellow and droops.","Roots drink water and goodness from the soil. Leaves catch sunlight and take in air. Together they make food for the plant. Try the activity below.","Try it: Grow two bean sprouts. Put one in a bright place and one in a dark cupboard. Give both water. Look after 5 days.","Tip: Sun, water, air, soil. Say it with 4 claps. Take away any one and the plant is in trouble.","Careful: Plants do not eat soil like food. They make their own food in the leaves. Fun fact: Plants give out oxygen for us to breathe."],["Tumbuhan ialah benda hidup, jadi ia memerlukan sesuatu untuk membesar. Tumbuhan perlukan cahaya matahari, air, udara dan tanah. Tanpanya ia menjadi lemah dan boleh mati.","Pokok dalam pasu di tepi tingkap mendapat cahaya matahari dan membesar hijau dan tinggi. Pokok yang dilupakan berhari-hari dalam almari gelap menjadi kuning dan layu.","Akar menyerap air dan zat daripada tanah. Daun menangkap cahaya matahari dan mengambil udara. Bersama-sama mereka membuat makanan untuk tumbuhan. Cuba aktiviti di bawah.","Cuba ini: Tanam dua taugeh. Letak satu di tempat terang dan satu di dalam almari gelap. Beri air kepada kedua-duanya. Lihat selepas 5 hari.","Tip: Matahari, air, udara, tanah. Sebut dengan 4 tepukan. Ambil satu daripadanya dan tumbuhan akan bermasalah.","Awas: Tumbuhan tidak makan tanah seperti makanan. Ia membuat makanan sendiri dalam daun. Fakta menarik: Tumbuhan mengeluarkan oksigen untuk kita bernafas."]],
"s_force": [["A force is a push or a pull. A force can make things start moving, stop, move faster or slower, change direction or change shape.","You push a door to open it and pull a drawer to open it. You kick a ball with a push. In tug of war, both teams pull on the rope.","Squash a lump of clay and it changes shape. A strong wind pushes sails and a magnet pulls a paper clip. We do not always need hands.","Try it: Find 5 things at home to push and 5 things to pull. Does a big push move a heavy box more than a small push?","Tip: Away is push, towards is pull. Remember: push goes away, pull comes close.","Fun fact: Gravity is a pull. It pulls everything down towards the Earth, so a dropped spoon falls and does not float away."],["Daya ialah tolakan atau tarikan. Daya boleh membuat benda mula bergerak, berhenti, bergerak lebih laju atau lebih perlahan, menukar arah atau menukar bentuk.","Kamu tolak pintu untuk membukanya dan tarik laci untuk membukanya. Kamu menendang bola dengan tolakan. Dalam tarik tali, kedua-dua pasukan menarik tali.","Tekan segumpal tanah liat dan ia berubah bentuk. Angin kuat menolak layar dan magnet menarik klip kertas. Kita tidak selalu perlukan tangan.","Cuba ini: Cari 5 benda di rumah untuk ditolak dan 5 benda untuk ditarik. Adakah tolakan kuat menggerakkan kotak berat lebih jauh daripada tolakan lemah?","Tip: Menjauh ialah tolak, mendekat ialah tarik. Ingat: tolak pergi jauh, tarik datang dekat.","Fakta menarik: Graviti ialah tarikan. Ia menarik semua benda ke bawah menuju Bumi, jadi sudu yang jatuh tidak terapung pergi."]],
"s_matter": [["Everything around us is made of matter. Matter comes in three states: solid, liquid and gas. Each one behaves in its own way.","A solid keeps its own shape, like a block, a book or a stone. A liquid flows and takes the shape of its container. Juice is round in a cup and tall in a bottle.","A gas has no shape and spreads out to fill any space. Air in a balloon spreads to fill it. Bubbles in fizzy drinks are gas.","Try it: Sort 6 things in your house into solid, liquid or gas. Pour water into different containers and watch its shape change.","Tip: Solid stays, liquid flows, gas spreads. Say it like a chant.","Careful: Air is not nothing. It is a gas. Fun fact: Steam is water as a gas, and it is hot. Never touch steam."],["Semua benda di sekeliling kita diperbuat daripada jirim. Jirim ada tiga keadaan: pepejal, cecair dan gas. Setiap satu berkelakuan dengan caranya sendiri.","Pepejal mengekalkan bentuknya sendiri, seperti blok, buku atau batu. Cecair mengalir dan mengambil bentuk bekasnya. Jus bulat dalam cawan dan tinggi dalam botol.","Gas tidak mempunyai bentuk dan menyebar untuk memenuhi mana-mana ruang. Udara dalam belon menyebar untuk memenuhinya. Gelembung dalam minuman bergas ialah gas.","Cuba ini: Asingkan 6 benda di rumah kamu kepada pepejal, cecair atau gas. Tuang air ke dalam bekas berlainan dan lihat bentuknya berubah.","Tip: Pepejal kekal, cecair mengalir, gas menyebar. Sebut seperti cogan kata.","Awas: Udara bukan tiada apa-apa. Ia ialah gas. Fakta menarik: Wap ialah air dalam bentuk gas dan ia panas. Jangan sentuh wap."]],
"s_chain": [["A food chain shows who eats whom. It starts with plants, which make their own food from sunlight. Animals eat plants or other animals to get energy.","In a padi field: padi grains feed a rat, a snake eats the rat and an eagle eats the snake. Padi, rat, snake, eagle is a food chain.","Another chain: tiny plants in a pond are eaten by small fish, small fish are eaten by a big fish and a kingfisher eats the big fish.","Try it: Draw a food chain with 4 boxes and arrows. Start with a plant and the Sun. Show it to someone and say who eats whom.","Tip: The arrow means is eaten by. It points to the one that eats. Plants are at the start of the chain.","Fun fact: The Sun gives energy to plants, so nearly every food chain starts with the Sun. Careful: Remove one link and the others are affected."],["Rantai makanan menunjukkan siapa makan siapa. Ia bermula dengan tumbuhan yang membuat makanan sendiri daripada cahaya matahari. Haiwan makan tumbuhan atau haiwan lain untuk mendapat tenaga.","Di sawah padi: bijirin padi dimakan tikus, ular memakan tikus dan helang memakan ular. Padi, tikus, ular, helang ialah satu rantai makanan.","Satu lagi rantai: tumbuhan kecil di kolam dimakan ikan kecil, ikan kecil dimakan ikan besar dan burung pekaka memakan ikan besar.","Cuba ini: Lukis rantai makanan dengan 4 kotak dan anak panah. Mulakan dengan tumbuhan dan Matahari. Tunjuk kepada seseorang dan sebut siapa makan siapa.","Tip: Anak panah bermaksud dimakan oleh. Ia menunjuk kepada yang makan. Tumbuhan berada di awal rantai.","Fakta menarik: Matahari memberi tenaga kepada tumbuhan, jadi hampir semua rantai makanan bermula dengan Matahari. Awas: Buang satu mata rantai dan yang lain terjejas."]]
};
